title: telegram editMessageText fails MESSAGE_TOO_LONG when status edits exceed 4096 chars
updated_at: "2026-09-28T02:55:46Z"
---
Observed in daemon.log: 35x WARN "Telegram editMessageText failed (HTTP 400, chat_id=<id>, message_id=11001): {\"ok\":false,\"error_code\":400,\"description\":\"Bad Request: MESSAGE_TOO_LONG\"}". Long agent status/edit updates exceed Telegram's 4096-char message limit and the edit is dropped.

Decisions (already made):
- Pre-truncate the editMessageText payload to the 4096 limit at a safe boundary (prefer reusing any existing split/truncate helpers in src/telegram_format.ml), appending a short ellipsis marker when truncated.
- Apply the same guard on the sendMessage path only if it is not already guarded (audit; sendMessage already appears to split - verify and leave alone if so).
- Keep HTML entity escaping intact when truncating (do not cut inside an entity/tag if avoidable; a conservative codepoint-boundary cut plus marker is acceptable).

Acceptance criteria:
1. Unit test: an edit payload > 4096 chars is truncated to <= 4096 and still sends (mock transport sees no MESSAGE_TOO_LONG).
2. Truncation marker present so the user knows content was cut.
3. sendMessage behavior unchanged if already safe (regression test if touched).
4. make test green; fmt-check clean.